// A character outside the lexical grammar. GRAMMAR.md section 1 names what a token is;
// an at-sign is none of it, so the lexer has no token for it. It sits BETWEEN two lawful
// declarations on purpose: a stray character inside a declaration would also upset the
// parse, and what a parser reports after that is recovery, which this suite does not
// pin. Here the character is skipped and both declarations read normally.
// Expected: UNEXPECTED_CHARACTER

DEFINE SCREEN ledger_overview (
  SATISFIES [READ]
)

@

DEFINE SCREEN invoice_detail (
  SATISFIES [READ]
)
